cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Heavy Quark Two-Body Energy Predictor"
abstract: >
  A surrogate neural-network web application that predicts the bound-state
  energy levels (E₀–E₃) of heavy-quark two-body systems using the
  Meng–Wang–Oka (MWO) potential model. The network is trained on data
  generated by TwoBody.jl and served as a static web page via TensorFlow.js.
authors:
  - family-names: "Jantarasaengaram"
    given-names: "Poompat"
repository-code: "https://github.com/poomj/heavyquark"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-03"
keywords:
  - heavy quarks
  - two-body problem
  - surrogate model
  - neural network
  - TensorFlow.js
  - quantum mechanics
references:
